  "narrative": "H19 response deadline: independent validation R20 is signed +0.817 with validation interval +0.715 to +0.918, confirming discovery R17 (+0.832). Because H19 is direction -1, the positive signed value corresponds to a raw negative contrast: feature_037=1 is associated with a more negative outcome_001 score, i.e. stronger dependency, by about 0.8 composite units. This is far above the 0.15-unit threshold and robust under the independent-validation uncertainty accounting. I therefore reassess H19 as accepted and keep it closed. H55: discovery R36 was a borderline positive interaction estimate (+0.210; 95% interval +0.019 to +0.400), but validation R43 is +0.262 with an independent interval +(-0.040) to +0.565. The validation interval crosses zero and its lower bound is well below the 0.15-unit practical threshold. Although both point estimates are positive and suggestive, the combined discovery-plus-validation evidence does not establish a scientifically meaningful positive feature_002-by-feature_010 interaction, especially after several interaction contrasts were examined. I therefore reassess H55 as rejected/closed as an accepted claim, while interpreting this as unsupported evidence for amplification rather than proof of no effect. H54 remains rejected because the same evidence does not support the negative-direction interaction. Current main supported associations are: feature_037 positive status associated with stronger dependency (validated H19), feature_002 positive status associated with weaker dependency (validated H24), and feature_010 positive status associated with weaker dependency (accepted H16 but not yet independently validated). Pairwise interactions involving feature_037 are not supported (H46/H47 and H52/H53), and feature_002-by-feature_010 is now not robustly supported. The feature_040 median-stratum main effects still indicate that the three top associations persist across clinical log_pfs strata, but formal feature_040 effect modification is not yet settled. The most informative next analysis is to run the registered formal feature_040 interaction claims H62-H67, especially the feature_002-by-feature_040 contrast suggested by R39/R40, together with the residual marker tests H74-H77 in the joint top-predictor-negative stratum. If residual markers show large precise effects, they become new validation candidates. If a feature_040 interaction is meaningful, the top main effects should be interpreted as context-dependent dataset-specific associations. In the next appraise, request validation of H16 to strengthen the third major main association. All conclusions remain associations in this supplied dataset and do not establish causality, mechanism, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Updated conclusions after H55 validation: Accepted dataset-specific main predictors remain feature_037 positive -> more negative outcome_001/stronger dependency (H19, validated); feature_002 positive -> less negative outcome_001/weaker dependency (H24, validated); feature_010 positive -> less negative outcome_001/weaker dependency (H16, accepted but unvalidated). Do not request more validation for H55: validation did not confirm a robust positive feature_002-by-feature_010 interaction; treat as unsupported, not proven absent. Formal interactions involving feature_037 are rejected. Feature_040 median-stratum main effects persist but formal interaction testing is pending. Next analyze priorities: (1) H62-H67 formal feature_040 median interactions, especially H64 for feature_002, because R39/R40 suggest possible modest amplification in the high-log_pfs stratum; (2) residual marker tests H74-H77 for feature_001 and feature_003 within the joint top-negative stratum. In next appraise, if new discovery evidence is present, request validation of H16. Before running broad untested binary predictor scans H25-H36, register opposite-direction claims so that both stronger and weaker dependency directions can be evaluated without post hoc sign selection. If H74/H76 show threshold-exceeding precise effects, propose corresponding opposite/refinement and validation candidates. If residual scans are null, support the interpretation that the currently identified predictors dominate the measurable dependency architecture in this supplied dataset. All claims remain association-only.",
